\node[above left] at (P) {\$P\$};\node[above right] at (Q) {\$Q\$};\node[below right] at (S) {\$S\$};\node[below left] at (T) {\$T\$};\node[anchor=west] at ($(M)+(0.08,0)$) {\$M\$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Look for pairs of equal angles, and give a reason for each.
$\angle PMQ=\angle SMT$ (vertically opposite angles)
$\angle QPM=\angle TSM$ (alternate angles, $PQ\parallel ST$)
Therefore $\triangle PQM\sim\triangle STM$, since at least two pairs of corresponding angles are equal (AAA).
Guided practice:
Proposed question: Identify why the two triangles are similar
(with a diagram)
Answers: $\angle NKP=\angle LKM$ (common angle) and $\angle KNP=\angle KLM$ (corresponding angles, $NP\parallel LM$), so the triangles are similar by AAA.
Comparison score: 50.

[Pedagogy audit v2 · New teaching] The booklet teaches the four similarity tests but never shows how to find an unknown side by matching corresponding sides, writing the proportion and solving it. A worked example after the identify exercise would give students the method before the practice questions.
Worked example: For this pair of triangles:

**a** Identify why the two triangles are similar

**b** find the value of $x$
**a** $\angle A=\angle D$ and $\angle B=\angle E$ (marked). Therefore $\triangle ABC\sim\triangle DEF$, since at least two pairs of corresponding angles are equal.

**b** $EF$ corresponds to $BC$, and $DE$ corresponds to $AB$.
$$\begin{align*}\frac{x}{8}&=\frac{9}{6}\\x&=8\times\frac{9}{6}\\x&=12\text{ cm}\end{align*}$$
Guided practice:
Proposed question: For this pair of triangles:
a) Identify why the two triangles are similar
b) find the value of $x$
(with a diagram)
Answers: a) At least two pairs of equal corresponding angles (AAA).; b) $x=14\text{ cm}$
Comparison score: 39.
